{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794761902,"nonce":"L8igRnW9i5U00glIkHfX0IeEWEI=","message":"Window trace of the cn demo, 84 s of use (BLINC_MOTION_TRACE, build with d0a0e2d1 and f56b854e).\n\n- 1,843 frames drawn: 723 served from the cache, 1,120 painted in full. A cached frame costs 0.43 ms in the render phase (0.58 ms in all); a full paint 11.8 ms median in the render phase, 10 to 17 ms by bucket. The style phase is 24 us median in both: what a full paint costs is the render, not the style pass.\n- During a stretch of CSS animation only (the indeterminate bar on screen, no input) the frames were all cache frames at about 50 a second, 0.57 ms each, which is a few percent of a core. Stretches of the same CSS activity with full paints (e.g. 28 s: 99 of 144) cost 11 ms each. Nothing in the frame record separates them; the fast-path gate in present.rs has more terms than the trace records.\n- Hover, with no redraw signal asking, produced about 120 full paints in two seconds (the 38 s bucket).\n- Overlay open: 12 frames asked by overlay_css, mixed with full paints.\n\nThen: a full paint of the demo went from 9.2 ms to 4.8 ms (6ece7d6, d-commit \"a full paint walks absolute bounds down, not up\").\n\nNext measurement to take: record which term of try_fast_paint blocks each full frame, so the trace says why, as it now says which.","files":null}]}